Original commit body from 443bf5506d6198964c1b21d7a0910c616654eecb:

A Kotlin repo that reads a socket and writes the bytes to disk returned rc=0
`confirmed` with 93 catalogued sinks, dataflow_capable=False and zero findings.
The coverage gate asked only "did this language produce ANY call edge", and one
intra-repo call was enough to look covered.

`verify_claims.method_starved_modules` now also asks whether any method-construct
call edge landed in a method-keyed catalogue module the repo actually CALLS.
Kotlin emits the `File(...)` constructor but no edge at all for `.writeText`, so
`java.io.File` is starved and the verdict degrades honestly. The boundary gate and
the taint gate share the one predicate.

Four candidates were measured over six fixtures before any code changed
(scripts/measure-blind-language-signal.py, in-repo). "Non-first-party dsts" does
not discriminate — Kotlin's intra-repo dst path slot is RELATIVE and
is_first_party_callable_dst requires an absolute one. "Any method-construct edge"
catches Kotlin but downgrades a pure-computation Python repo that calls nothing
external, which is the blanket-downgrade failure mode that made `confirmed`
unreachable in this gate's first version.

The first version of the shipped predicate was ALSO wrong and real repos caught
it: JS/TS populate call_construct on ZERO of 4,872 call edges, so it reported fs,
console and process starved on both JavaScript repos measured. The check now
abstains per-language for any analyzer that never stamps the field — None (could
not check) is not empty (checked, found none). Filed as INV-gijis.

Direction on a real 14-language repo (sherpa-onnx): 12 of 14 languages pass; the
two catches name specific modules. The java catch was new — java.nio.file.Files'
methods are STATIC but catalogued kind=method, so the whole Files sink surface is
unmatchable (INV-suril).

Also fixes a pre-existing test-isolation defect this work exposed:
ensure_def_use_extractors_registered restored the def/use registry by importing
modules for their decorator side effect, which sys.modules caching makes a no-op
after clear_def_use_extractors() — so it returned True having restored nothing and
every language read dataflow_capable=False. Two test_taint_recall_corpus failures
appeared only in full-suite runs and passed at every narrower scope. The first fix
keyed on "registry empty" and did not work, because a partial restore leaves it
populated but missing javascript; the guard now compares against the full expected
set, learned from the first successful registration rather than hardcoded.
Filed as INV-votoj, which also records that ddg_build.clear_ddg_languages() has
the same unguarded shape.

Full suite: 22,255 passed / 0 failed / 100% coverage; all 6 packages 100% in
isolation; mypy strict ratchet 672 (delta +0).

